  url = {https://doi.org/10.1109/icmlca66850.2025.11336530},
  howpublished = {International Conference on Machine Learning and Computer Application (ICMLCA)},
  annotation = {中文辅助译名：SmokeSAM：基于SAM和LoRA微调的车辆黑烟分割},
  abstract = {Vision-based vehicle smoke segmentation focuses on identifying smoke regions in video frames, which is a critical task for intelligent surveillance systems. This paper introduces a novel approach for segmenting vehicle black smoke in images using a vision model-based method. Recently, the Segment Anything Model (SAM) has gained significant attention in the field of computer vision due to its exceptional generalization capabilities and robust architectural design, powered by pretraining on a large-scale dataset with over 1 billion annotations. In this study, we in-vestigate the application of SAM for vehicle black smoke segmentation. However, experimental results reveal that SAM struggles with smoke detection and segmentation tasks, underperforming compared to other foun-dational models. To address this limitation, we propose a fine-tuning strategy using Low-Rank Adaptation (LoRA) to enhance SAM's image encoder. Our method, SmokeSAM, implements this by adapting the image encoder with LoRA and fine-tuning the mask decoder, which enables fully au-tomatic, prompt-free segmentation. To facilitate this research, we introduce Smoke _ Sd,a new dataset specifically for vehicle black smoke. Trained on Smoke_SD and the public PoVSSeg dataset, SmokeSAM achieves substantial improvements over state-of-the-art segmentation methods. Extensive experiments validate the ef-fectiveness of our approach. Furthermore, because SmokeSAM fine-tunes only a small fraction of SAM's parameters, it demon-s},
}

